From: arch-m4 project
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: replay the existing T6040 USB2 host sequence

The private powered flag survives generic phy_power_off(), because the
host-only slice deliberately has no hardware power_off callback. It then
suppresses the next power_on after DWC3's cable disconnect/reconnect cycle.

Rely on generic PHY power_count to suppress duplicate live power_on calls.
Drop the sticky private state so a later balanced power_on replays exactly
the existing host sequence. No MMIO operations, inverse sequence or
power_off callback are added.

Local candidate against Wallace 55f116dd0e0f28d1412c6be728a101f7d861c473's
experimental T6040 USB2-only PHY patch. Native reconnect remains unverified.

--- a/drivers/phy/apple/t6040-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/t6040-usb2.c
@@ -58,7 +58,6 @@
 	struct phy *phy;
 	struct mutex lock;
 	enum phy_mode mode;
-	bool powered;
 };
 
 static inline void t6040_usb2_mask32(void __iomem *reg, u32 mask, u32 set)
@@ -88,9 +87,6 @@
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 
 	guard(mutex)(&tphy->lock);
-	if (tphy->powered && tphy->mode != mode)
-		return -EBUSY;
-
 	tphy->mode = mode;
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -104,8 +100,13 @@
 
 	if (tphy->mode != PHY_MODE_USB_HOST)
 		return -EINVAL;
-	if (tphy->powered)
-		return 0;
+
+	/*
+	 * Generic PHY power_count suppresses duplicate live power_on calls.
+	 * Replay this known sequence after a balanced off/on so a Type-C PD
+	 * repeater reset cannot leave the previous initialization cached.
+	 * There is still no inferred hardware power-off sequence.
+	 */
 
 	/*
 	 * AppleT6040TypeCPhy::eusb2phy_init(false, false), in exact order.
@@ -153,7 +154,6 @@
 			  T6040_USB2_USBCTL_MODE,
 			  T6040_USB2_USBCTL_MODE_HOST);
 
-	tphy->powered = true;
 	dev_info(tphy->dev, "USB2 host sequence complete\n");
 	return 0;
 }
